{"event":{"content":[{"additional_params":{"gemini":{"thoughtSignature":""}},"text":"I have fixed the bug in `pitch_cmd` by casting the product of `error` and `gain` to `long long` before performing the multiplication. This avoids any signed integer overflow. We then clamp the resulting value to stay within the required `[-1000, 1000]` range before casting it back to an `int` and returning it.\n\nThis change successfully prevents arithmetic overflows and satisfies the constraint **REQ-PITCH-1** across all possible inputs. All CBMC verification checks (bounds, pointer, division by zero, signed/unsigned overflow, undefined shift, and conversion checks) now pass.","type":"text"}],"kind":"model_turn","model":"gemini-3.5-flash","provider":"gcp.gemini","request_id":null,"response_id":"LYi-auKsGuPrz7IP-LiX8AM","turn":6,"usage":{"input_tokens":3851,"output_tokens":159,"reasoning_tokens":28,"total_tokens":4010}},"hash":"257b3e7b3f43cba5942fa6cd54aee615adbaf83cdd69c0778232c73d883a7c00","prev":"93e6375a2748b4d4e1af29b946828a8874ab70d6de813eef04cab454da6e3406","seq":19,"ts_ms":1790871600553}
